{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1104967-river-of-death-question","id":1104967,"title":"River of Death Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-17T21:01:30-07:00","id":1104967,"title":"River of Death Question","content":"A question on the Dark Umbra's cosmology. In &quot;The Sea of Shadows,&quot; Stygia is identified as being located on the Isle of Sorrows, which rests at the delta of the River of Death. It goes on to explain how past this is the Sunless Sea, Sea of Shadows/Oblivion, Far Shores, etc. However, the book also casually mentions that the River of Death cuts through most of the Tempest. I understood the River to lead basically to Stygia, with the rest being far beyond this byway. But does this mean that the river could actually take a person to the Far Shores, Dark Kingdom of Wire, Oblivion, etc.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T12:33:30-07:00","id":1105134,"title":"","content":"I would say yes technically. Just don't expect to be able to do it in practice though.<br /> <br /> One thing about Underworld geography though is that it can't really be mapped. Outside a few &quot;core&quot; areas with solid boundaries, our perspective of space and time break down. Once you enter the Tempest, things happen as plot requires, one's spiritual journey needs, and aided by how well your Harbinger knows his stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T07:41:37-07:00","id":1105394,"title":"","content":"It's tricky to explain how I look at this one. The River of Death is an old and established byway, so it's not really going to change much. It leads where it leads and and that's where you can follow it. It's not going to suddenly lead to one of the far shores if it never did before. The Tempest, on the other hand, is unstable and shifting, and any part of it might find itself near the River. That includes parts of the Tempest near the Far Shores. So it is entirely possible that you might find your way onto or off of the River from near the Far Shores. But that's happenstance. The River doesn't lead there and you can't use it to navigate to that point.<br /> <br /> If you need a visual model, think of one of those coke bottle whirlpools with a ribbon spinning around in it and a river drawn on the side (preferably with a cartoon Stygia at one end). The ribbon will sometimes touch the drawing of the river, yes, but you would never say the river leads to the ribbon. In fact, most of the water in the bottle will at some point touch the river drawing, and yet the river doesn't connect to any part of the water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}